{"step_index":11348,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T15:20:43Z","thinking":"Considering performance, calculating properties for large directories presents a challenge. The system could cache directory sizes and file counts for known massive directories to optimize speed. Single file property retrieval is quick, taking only a fraction of a second. The goal is to provide properties, focusing on folder size and file count as requested, avoiding unnecessary complexity.\n\n\nConsidering the user's preference for a simplified Windows 11-style properties dialog, the design should prioritize folder size and file count display.  A clean modal window with a clear header, relevant icons, and key details (type, location, size, and contents) will be implemented. The properties window should be accessible via right-click context menus on desktop and long-press on mobile, as well as an \"info\" icon in file view modes.\n\n\nAnalyzing the `server.py` file reveals the existing `handle_properties` function needs to be extended to serve the `/api/properties` endpoint. The current implementation handles file properties; extending it to directories necessitates calculating size and count recursively. Implementation will handle non-existent paths with an error response.\n\n\nA cache is being checked first, ensuring that recently retrieved directory properties are served from memory if available, optimizing for speed. If not cached, the system calculates directory size using a utility, falling back to a different method if the initial one fails. File and folder counts are then obtained using another utility, employing a fallback recursive method if timeouts or errors occur with the initial approach. Finally, all the retrieved information is compiled into a data structure for transmission.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport os, subprocess, time\\n\\ndef format_size(size_bytes):\\n    for unit in ['B', 'KB', 'MB', 'GB', 'TB']:\\n        if size_bytes < 1024.0:\\n            return f'{size_bytes:.2f} {unit}'\\n        size_bytes /= 1024.0\\n    return f'{size_bytes:.2f} PB'\\n\\ndef get_props(target_path):\\n    is_dir = os.path.isdir(target_path)\\n    name = os.path.basename(target_path) or target_path\\n    stat_res = os.stat(target_path)\\n    mtime_str = time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %I:%M %p', time.localtime(stat_res.st_mtime))\\n    if not is_dir:\\n        return {'name': name, 'size': format_size(stat_res.st_size), 'files': 1, 'folders': 0}\\n    try:\\n        size_out = subprocess.check_output(['du', '-sb', target_path], timeout=3.0).decode()\\n        size = int(size_out.split()[0])\\n    except Exception:\\n        size = 0\\n    try:\\n        f_out = subprocess.check_output(['find', target_path, '-type', 'f', '-printf', '.'], timeout=3.0).decode()\\n        files = f_out.count('.')\\n        d_out = subprocess.check_output(['find', target_path, '-type', 'd', '-printf', '.'], timeout=3.0).decode()\\n        folders = max(0, d_out.count('.') - 1)\\n    except Exception:\\n        files, folders = 0, 0\\n    return {'name': name, 'size': format_size(size), 'bytes': f'{size:,}', 'files': files, 'folders': folders, 'mtime': mtime_str}\\n\\nprint('Props .gemini:', get_props('/home/azureuser/IrakIroan/.gemini'))\\nprint('Props config:', get_props('/home/azureuser/IrakIroan/config'))\\nprint('Props README.md:', get_props('/home/azureuser/IrakIroan/README.md'))\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/home/azureuser\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Testing properties logic\"","toolSummary":"\"Test properties function in Python\""}}]}
